COMMENTARY, CONVERSATION AND CHATTER
&hTab;Well, now.  There are no “No. 1s” in the Final Four this year. Not since the eighties has such a No. 1-seed been playing for College Basketball’s championship in Indianapolis.  Everybody is just gone wild over George Mason, the tiny little school from nearby Washington, D.C.  These Patriots have beaten North Carolina, Michigan State, and Connecticut to get to play at the “big dance”. And it is true that this team has come back from deficits and played the kind of defense that only championship teams play.  And everybody is now aware of just who and what George Mason university is. Appropriately called “the Cinderella team”, George Mason will play for but not become the Champion.  That title will go to Shaq’s old school, Louisiana State university.  Do look for a good matchup between Thomas and Davis.

