Chatter, Commentary, Conversation
&hTab;Well, you know we have some Monday Niters who got some bad news over the holidays.  It wasn’t about the Chiefs and their playoff hopes.  It wasn’t about how Denver squeaked by the Bengals in a thriller.  It was about their favorite hang-out, the infamous “6902”.  A shooting, resulting in a murder, was recorded.  Then, right after that, the place burned up.  What a week for the well-attended night club.  Booker cried.  Carl is just not himself, at all.  And Charles is clearly at a loss for words.  Several neighbors have commented that the club is usually trouble-free and attracted both young and old.  And it is significant because what happened there was more newsworthy than what is happening with our last-chance Chiefs.
&hTab;Here’s the scene, if the Chiefs are to win a spot in the playoffs.  First, they must beat Jacksonville on Sunday, out at Arrowhead.  Some think they will because usually (I say usually) the Chiefs win at home.  But, in addition to a must-win for the Chiefs’, both San Francisco, Tennessee and Pittsburgh must win.  Then, the Chiefs would backdoor into the last playoff spot.  But, I have a question for you.
&hTab;Why is it we always have to struggle our way into the playoffs, especially here in December?  Why couldn’t we just have beaten weak Cleveland and crippled Miami? Then, we would be just like the Jets…already in.  But, that Herman Edwards and that no-named offensive coordinator just blew it all…with their senseless, play-ground play-calling.  Bottom line, prepare yourself for a Chiefs’ loss  Sunday or for Denver and Cincinnati to win.  Any one of those scenarios will spell the end of the season for Kansas City.  And just think, Herm has already started talking about 2007 and how he is going to stick with Tricky Trent Green.  And just like always, the Chiefs will soon be talking smack and lament that they were two or three plays away from post-season competition.  Crap.
&hTab;Anybody know when the “6902” is gonna re-open?&hTab;
