&hTab;Donnelly Colege will offer a Scholarship Information Night on Monday, Feb. 16, from 6:30-8:30 p.m., in the first floor Meeting Room.  Participants need to make a reservation by calling (913) 621-8700.
&hTab;At the session, students will learn how to get free money to attend Donnelly College.  Presenters will explain how to apply for Presidential and Bloch Scholarships which cover tuition, fees and books.  They will also learn about federal Pell Grants and Kansas comprehensive Grants for low-income students.  All students with a GPA of 2.5 or above, who participate in the Scholarship Night, will be awarded a minimum scholarship of $500 to be used at Donnelly College for tuition not covered by grants.
&hTab;“Limited financial resources are no obstacle for attending college,” said Sister Mary Agnes Patterson, Donnelly Vice-President.  “There are grants and scholarships available for those who qualify.  And starting at a local college like Donnelly saves students the cost of living in a dorm and allows them to work part-time.”&hTab;
